**How to implement.** The key split's matched / unmatched table in the Data step, with Apply and Cancel (001 §O 'Data dialog: … the key split with a matched / unmatched table'; 001 §O 'Automation': `DataSplitKeyColumn`; .spec-md §10.3 identify → confirm, §10.5 Apply / Cancel share a row with a gap and distinct positive and negative colours; the S9.3 brief). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs` (step 323): when `model.dataSplitOpt` is `Some s` (step 319), under the Split verb, a bordered vertical panel holding: a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `dataSplitKeyColumn` with `Split <the file's leaf> by '<s.key>' through '<s.profile>'`; one row per group of `s.split.groups`, in order, carrying `dataSplitGroupRow group.key` and reading `<key> — <n> point(s) — ` then, for `ExperimentForGroup name`, `→ <name>`; for `SetupOfferForGroup offer`, a box carrying `dataSplitOfferToggle group.key` labelled `Create <offer.experiment> over '<offer.setup.name>'`, followed by ` (new setup)` when `model.kitSetups` lacks the setup, on the positive background when `s.creating` holds the key and in the verb look otherwise, sending `ToggleSplitOffer group.key`; and for `GroupWithoutMatch problem`, `unmatched — <problem.describe>` in the message colour; then one horizontal row of `Apply split` (`dataSplitApplyButton`, the positive action look, sending `MatchByTemplate`, step 320, disabled when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlWithheld`) and, after a gap, `Cancel` (`dataSplitCancelButton`, the negative action look, sending `CancelDataSplit`), the `MaterialsWindowView` action buttons step 309 uses. A label never sits in a horizontal `StackPanel` beside a wrapping one (AGENTS.md: dock it in a `DockPanel`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Data step group (step 323), each with a one-line doc: `dataSplitKeyColumn` (`"DataSplitKeyColumn"`), `dataSplitApplyButton` (`"DataSplitApplyButton"`) and `dataSplitCancelButton` (`"DataSplitCancelButton"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type DataRowKey with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (its text); on `ConstructorUiId`, `static member dataSplitGroupRow (key : DataRowKey) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataSplitGroup_<key>`) and `static member dataSplitOfferToggle (key : DataRowKey) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataSplitOffer_<key>`), as `attachDataFile` is keyed by its experiment; and `type DataSplitError with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, its `describe`. No other control or message is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs`, `module DataStepTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended to the compile list after `KitWindowTests.fs` with no comment; its views are mounted over the inverse model (`initInverse`, as `KitWindowTests` builds it, step 184) loaded from a folder kit under the class's test directory opened read-write, with `E1` committed, as `KitWindowTests` mounts the kit window (step 242), and a test-local `DataSplitState` over `phone.csv` by `experiment` through `Phone ROI CSV` whose groups are `K1` (2 points) matched to `E1`, `K2` (1) offered the new setup `Bench B` and the experiment `K2`, and `K3` (1) unmatched with `SplitKeyNameErr`. `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the Data step's ids so far (`FlowDataStep`, `DataStepPanel`, `DataSplitFileButton`, `DataSplitKeyColumn`, `DataSplitApplyButton`, `DataSplitCancelButton`, `DataSplitGroup_K1`, `DataSplitOffer_K2`). `the split panel names its key column and lists each group matched, offered or unmatched, with Apply and Cancel in one row`: `dataSplitKeyColumn` reads `Split phone.csv by 'experiment' through 'Phone ROI CSV'`; the three group rows read `→ E1`, `Create K2 over 'Bench B' (new setup)` and a text starting `unmatched —`; only `K2` has a toggle; `dataSplitApplyButton` and `dataSplitCancelButton` have equal tops, Cancel right of Apply with a gap between. `pressing an offer ticks it, and Cancel forgets the split`: over a `HostWindow` running `Program.mkSimple` of the model with `updateTableAndElementRotation` and `dataStepView`, pressing the toggle's centre leaves `creating` [`K2`] and the toggle on the positive background, and pressing Cancel's centre leaves `dataSplitOpt` `None` and no split panel. With trait `ui-smoke`, `the Data step renders a split and Apply split attaches its matched group`: over a folder kit holding `E1` and its split by `SplitByColumn` of a test-local Phone ROI file whose rows all carry `E1`'s name, the rendered Data step shows the panel, and pressing `dataSplitApplyButton` leaves E1 mapped by `Phone ROI CSV` to the rows of its key and the panel gone.

**Acceptance.** After the split panel lands, the Data step MUST show a pending split's key column and each group matched, offered (with its toggle) or unmatched (with its reason), with Apply split and Cancel in one row, sending `ToggleSplitOffer`, `MatchByTemplate` and `CancelDataSplit` under the stable ids of `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the Data step renders a split and Apply split attaches its matched group`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the split panel names its key column and lists each group matched, offered or unmatched, with Apply and Cancel in one row` and `pressing an offer ticks it, and Cancel forgets the split`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.
